# IAM policy for Hostinger S3 access (operator)

Attach to a dedicated IAM user. **Do not** use root credentials on the VPS.

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "BankAppDurablePrefix",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:DeleteObject",
        "s3:ListBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::traxiproducts-finances-bank-app-data-eu-west-2",
        "arn:aws:s3:::traxiproducts-finances-bank-app-data-eu-west-2/bank-state/prod/*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Sid": "HermesBackupPrefixOptional",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::traxiproducts-finances-bank-app-data-eu-west-2",
        "arn:aws:s3:::traxiproducts-finances-bank-app-data-eu-west-2/hermes-backup/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Includes `data/truelayer-feed-cache/` under `bank-state/prod/`.

Store access keys in `production-env.local.sh` on the VPS only.
